    "text": "The equilibrium constant for the given reaction is approximately <math><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>–</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math><br />\r<br />\r<math> <mrow> <msubsup> <mrow> <mtext>HPO</mtext></mrow> <mn>4</mn> <mrow> <mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo></mrow> </msubsup> <mfenced> <mrow> <mtext>aq</mtext></mrow> </mfenced><mtext>&nbsp;</mtext><mo>+</mo><msubsup> <mrow> <mtext>HCO</mtext></mrow> <mn>3</mn> <mo>−</mo> </msubsup> <mtext>&nbsp;</mtext><mfenced> <mrow> <mtext>aq</mtext></mrow> </mfenced><mo>⇌</mo><msub> <mtext>H</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msub> <msubsup> <mrow> <mtext>PO</mtext></mrow> <mn>4</mn> <mo>−</mo> </msubsup> <mfenced> <mrow> <mtext>aq</mtext></mrow> </mfenced><mo>+</mo><msubsup> <mrow> <mtext>CO</mtext></mrow> <mn>3</mn> <mrow> <mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo></mrow> </msubsup> <mfenced> <mrow> <mtext>aq</mtext></mrow> </mfenced></mrow> </math><br />\r<br />\rWhich is strongest conjugate base in the given reaction?"
